<article class="env-lemma" id="0BLT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BLT">Lemma <span data-tag="0BLT">51.12.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $j : U \to X$ be the inclusion of an open subscheme with complement $Z$. Let $n \geq 0$ be an integer. If $R^ pj_*\mathcal{O}_ U$ is coherent for $0 \leq p < n$, then the same is true for $R^ pj_*\mathcal{F}$, $0 \leq p < n$ for any finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_ U$-module $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The question is local on $X$, hence we may assume $X$ is affine. Say $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ and $Z = V(I)$. Via Lemma <a href="/tag/0BK0" data-tag="0BK0">51.8.2</a> our lemma follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0BPY" data-tag="0BPY">51.7.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>